85	    /// Optional precomputed 4096-head NARS truth tables (TD-INT-10).
86	    ///
87	    /// When present, the cascade can look up Pearl 2³ + DK + Plasticity +
88	    /// Truth at dispatch time without paying for a runtime NARS engine.
89	    /// Lives in `causal-edge` (zero-dep), so attaching it does NOT pull
90	    /// the planner into shader-driver.
91	    pub(crate) nars_tables: Option<Arc<NarsTables>>,
92	    /// Transitional per-mailbox routing surface (slice A2).
93	    ///
94	    /// Consumers can opt into per-mailbox routing by inserting
95	    /// `MailboxSoA<1024>` instances here via the builder's
96	    /// `with_mailbox` method. The singleton `Arc<BindSpace>` (above)
97	    /// is unchanged — this field is purely additive and does not alter
98	    /// any existing dispatch semantics. Removed at cutover (plan S3).
99	    pub(crate) mailboxes: std::collections::HashMap<MailboxId, MailboxSoA<1024>>,
100	    /// Persistent rung-elevation state (`RungElevator`) across dispatch
101	    /// cycles. Each `run()` call is "one cycle" per this module's own
102	    /// docstring ("emits one CycleFingerprint per cycle — the unit of
103	    /// thought"); the elevator lives here — same `RwLock`-guarded,
104	    /// updated-every-cycle pattern as `awareness` above — so that
105	    /// "sustained BLOCK elevates" (the policy `RungElevator::on_gate`
106	    /// documents) can actually observe more than one gate. A
107	    /// per-call-local elevator would reset every dispatch and could
108	    /// never accumulate a streak. Reset to the dispatch's requested
109	    /// base whenever `ShaderDispatch::rung` changes between calls.
110	    pub(crate) rung_elevator: RwLock<RungElevator>,
111	}
